Patch 080 — extend-flashinfer-prefill-route (net-new 2026-11-12, the CUDA form of R9700 RAD-10c / patch 131)

On the Triton backend a cold prefill chunk is bound by extend_attention_fwd (Flint: 14 full-attention
layers per rank read the whole prefix for every 8192-row chunk; the 35 SWA layers are ~4 % of that).
flashinfer's paged prefill kernel does the same attention at x0.68-0.73 of the Triton launch on sm_86
and reads the fp8_e5m2 pool directly. Route a single-sequence causal EXTEND of
>= SGLANG_EXTEND_FLASHINFER_MIN_ROWS rows (0 = off, the default) on a full-attention layer through
BatchPrefillWithPagedKVCacheWrapper over the pool: prefix kv_indices + out_cache_loc as one slot table
(page size 1; the chunk's K/V are already in the pool), learned sinks merged through the returned LSE
(o *= sigmoid(lse*ln2 - sink)), planned once per forward batch. SWA layers, MLA, dLLM, custom masks,
soft-cap and score-mod stay on Triton; any exception declines the route for the process.

The slot table MUST be int32: an int64 table runs the same kernel at x1.76 (156 vs 89 ms at 123K
prefix x 8192 rows), which alone made the first served arm lose to Triton.

Flint served cold TTFT 2.94 / 23.2 / 67.0 s -> 2.69 / 18.3 / 50.0 s at 32K / 131K / 250K; TPOT
unchanged. Gate (two interleaved passes per arm): MMLU 292 vs 290 of 342, HumanEval 272 vs 272 of
328, haystack needle 196K-254K 25 vs 25 of 30. Receipts
benchmarks/profiling/prefill-flashinfer-route-2026-11-11/.

